WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:18.579
While she was at Aunt March's, Amy felt as though she were trapped in a pitch-black tunnel with no light beckoning to her at the end.

2
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:24.484
Until then, Amy had taken for granted the liveliness and warm affection of her family.

3
00:00:24.485 --> 00:00:31.356
How she missed the constant cheerful voices that seemed to fill the whole house all day long.

4
00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:38.181
"Did I ask you to stop?" Aunt March snapped when Amy, who was reading to her, paused to think about her family.

5
00:00:38.182 --> 00:00:42.980
"Stop!" screeched Polly as she took the cracker Aunt March offered her.

6
00:00:42.981 --> 00:00:49.152
"Forgive me, Aunt March. I'll continue . . . ," said Amy, returning her attention to the story.

7
00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:53.624
Aunt March might have been a nasty woman but she was not heartless.

8
00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:59.957
She was also worried about the fate of Beth, who she thought was witless but pure-hearted and innocent.

9
00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:05.126
"What have you heard about your sister?" This time she interrupted Amy's reading.

10
00:01:05.127 --> 00:01:08.745
Fiddling with a corner of the page she was reading, Amy replied,

11
00:01:08.746 --> 00:01:16.061
"Laurie says that Beth is coping better but her fever still has to drop, and she remains stable but weak."

12
00:01:16.062 --> 00:01:21.058
"And what of your Father? Will he be coming home soon?" asked Aunt March.

13
00:01:21.059 --> 00:01:30.262
Shaking her head, Amy said tearfully, "According to the last message we got, Father doesn't have the strength yet to make the journey home."

14
00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:36.641
"Rubbish! Your sister needs your mother more than he does," Aunt March remarked in a gruff voice.

15
00:01:36.642 --> 00:01:43.681
"Hannah says it's best not to tell Mother just yet, since there isn't much she can do here anyway," said Amy.

16
00:01:43.682 --> 00:01:53.692
Aunt March felt a pang in her heart as she watched Amy struggle to control her emotions. "I have a gift for you," she said in a kinder voice.

17
00:01:53.693 --> 00:02:00.686
Amy, wiping her tears (with a silk handkerchief, like a true lady), turned to her with curiosity.

18
00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:06.390
Aunt March held out a small green velvety box, which Amy slowly took from her.

19
00:02:06.391 --> 00:02:14.800
"Oh, Aunt March! I can't accept this," gasped Amy, holding up an emerald ring that flashed brilliantly in the light.

20
00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:24.830
"Yes, you can and you will, because I am giving it to you," Aunt March replied in a firm and strict voice that meant Amy should not try to argue with her.

21
00:02:24.831 --> 00:02:31.884
"It's beautiful," Amy said, her eyes dancing joyously as she put the ring on her middle finger.

22
00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:38.509
"I'm glad you like it. Now get back to the story," snapped Aunt March as she fed Polly another cracker.

23
00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:47.428
In addition to the ring, Aunt March promised Amy many more gifts as long as she remained obedient and found favor in the old lady's eyes.

24
00:02:47.429 --> 00:02:54.773
Upon his next daily visit, Amy promptly told this all to Laurie, who looked doubtful as he listened patiently.

25
00:02:54.774 --> 00:03:01.838
"Aunt March says emeralds are the most precious gems in the world," Amy said, sticking her hand out for him to admire.

26
00:03:01.839 --> 00:03:08.345
"It's very lovely, but don't you think you're a little too young for that?" asked Laurie with a frown.

27
00:03:08.346 --> 00:03:13.280
"Age means nothing if you are a true lady," Amy said knowingly.

28
00:03:13.281 --> 00:03:18.612
"Aunt March says I have the potential to become a respected woman of society."

29
00:03:18.613 --> 00:03:26.270
Laurie mumbled his opinion of Aunt March under his breath, but apparently Amy still had much more to say about material things.

30
00:03:26.271 --> 00:03:32.441
"Aunt March says I'm to have her pearl necklace, earrings, and diamond brooch after she dies!"

31
00:03:32.442 --> 00:03:36.461
"So you want her to die, do you?" Laurie asked nastily.

32
00:03:36.462 --> 00:03:41.219
Reddening in the face, Amy stuttered, "No. What I meant was . . ."

33
00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.821
"Do you want to know how Beth is or not?" Laurie asked rather harshly.

34
00:03:45.822 --> 00:03:56.307
Caught up in her own fantasy world, Amy had forgotten at that moment why Laurie was visiting her every day. "Of course, Laurie," she said, shamefaced.

35
00:03:56.308 --> 00:04:00.782
"Well, Beth is still . . . ," Laurie began more gently.

36
00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:03.919
As he spoke, Amy looked down at the ring.

37
00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:10.135
It didn't seem to shine as beautifully anymore, nor did the thought of a pearl necklace seem so appealing.

38
00:04:10.136 --> 00:04:16.230
The reality was that Beth was gravely sick, and death was no joking matter.

39
00:04:16.231 --> 00:04:20.286
After Laurie had left, Amy had a lot to think about.

40
00:04:20.287 --> 00:04:24.343
She stared at herself in the mirror for a very long time.

41
00:04:24.344 --> 00:04:30.041
Speaking to her reflection, Amy said, "One day you're going to die, too."

42
00:04:30.042 --> 00:04:34.386
"Can I take these things with me to my grave?" she wondered.

43
00:04:34.387 --> 00:04:41.398
Struck by the truth, she was forced to realize that her possessions would have no value to her once she were dead.

44
00:04:41.399 --> 00:04:50.640
After much soul searching, Amy decided to write a will, reasoning, "I want the people I love to have my things so they'll remember me by them."

45
00:04:50.641 --> 00:04:55.810
Armed with pen and paper, Amy began to write her last will and testament:

46
00:04:55.811 --> 00:05:04.135
I, Amy Curtis March, being of sound mind, do give all my possessions to the following persons named:

47
00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:12.454
To Father, all my drawings and sketches—those I kept since I was a little girl up to the ones he never saw.

48
00:05:12.455 --> 00:05:17.854
To Mother, all my clothes, except for the blue dress with pink and white flowers.

49
00:05:17.855 --> 00:05:21.218
That one I want Kitty to have. See below.

50
00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:31.311
To Meg, I give the emerald ring from Aunt March, because it is the perfect match for the color of your eyes. The velvet box I also give.

51
00:05:31.312 --> 00:05:40.185
To Jo, I give you all my hair ribbons so that when your hair grows long again, you will have beautiful, colorful ribbons to decorate it with.

52
00:05:40.186 --> 00:05:44.317
I also give you all my pens for you to write more stories with.

53
00:05:44.318 --> 00:05:52.505
To Beth (if she survives), all my dolls, my little play set of teacups, and pink slippers.

54
00:05:52.506 --> 00:06:00.647
To Laurie, I leave you my handkerchiefs with my initials embroidered on them so you will always remember me as a true lady.

55
00:06:00.648 --> 00:06:04.929
To Mr. Laurence, I give you my sculptures of your horses.

56
00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:10.061
I especially loved Harris, and there are two paintings of him that I hope you like.

57
00:06:10.062 --> 00:06:17.311
To Kitty Bryant, my blue dress with pink flowers and my bead necklace, which she always admired.

58
00:06:17.312 --> 00:06:22.478
To Hannah, my collection of seashells and the purple box I kept them in.

59
00:06:22.479 --> 00:06:27.136
And now, after leaving my possessions in the care of those I love and trust,

60
00:06:27.137 --> 00:06:36.259
I want to say how much I love you all and that each one of you has a special place in my heart. I trust we shall meet again.

61
00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:40.529
Signed: Amy Curtis March

62
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:45.811
When Amy finished writing her will, a peaceful calm came over her.

63
00:06:45.812 --> 00:06:54.063
She prayed, "God, if you allow Beth to live, I promise to be a better sister, daughter, and friend.

64
00:06:54.064 --> 00:06:58.575
Please give me the opportunity to prove that I have really changed."

65
00:06:58.576 --> 00:07:04.582
The next day when Laurie came, Amy showed him the will and asked him to sign it as a witness.

66
00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:09.665
Amused yet touched by Amy's maturity and thoughtfulness, Laurie agreed.

67
00:07:09.666 --> 00:07:15.605
Then he gave Amy the good news. "Mother March is coming home soon," he announced.

68
00:07:15.606 --> 00:07:20.592
"Beth? Does that mean . . ." Amy couldn't even say the words.

69
00:07:20.593 --> 00:07:27.503
Laurie took a deep breath and said, "I don't know, but Dr. Bangs said to send for your mother.

70
00:07:27.504 --> 00:07:31.301
The girls don't know yet. I want it to be a surprise."

71
00:07:31.302 --> 00:07:34.699
Amy was overjoyed that Mother was returning.

72
00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:40.989
She wondered whether her homecoming would be a happy or sad one.
